<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="165" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Invoice integrity (EB-D-200): hold, approval, AP export and spend decide only from server-written sources</title>
    <phase>4 Review</phase>
    <gate>165a: none. 165b: 164a integration branch (AddedLineIdFor) available.</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Approval, hold and payment inputs; access-adjacent (uac-r2 classes a/b/c); edits approval and AP export.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting integrity rules across approval, holds, AP export and spend; fail-closed design.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits InvoiceApprovalService and ApExportService; 165a and 165b run one after the other.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>EB-D-200; 164a-2 (AddedLineIdFor, on the 164a integration branch) for 165b</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ebilling, auth, integrity</tags>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Binding decisions: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/decisions-log.md EB-D-200 (owner, uac-r2 option D) and EB-D-101/103.
    The classes are uac-r2's.
    - (a) Written only on a path users cannot reach. Evidence: the live role privileges, plus the generic-path refusals.
    - (b) Field-secured, Writers only for writes.
    - (c) Re-derived or checked by the BFF, so that a user edit has no effect.
    Live dev facts (2026-11-06):
    - Spaarke Core User holds Write and Create on sprk_invoicesubmission and Write on sprk_invoice.
    - No user role holds Write on sprk_billingevent.
    - sprk_invoicesubmission.sprk_outcomereasoncode is not field-secured.
    Wording in commits, notes and the PR stays neutral: "decides only from server-written sources". Never describe a sequence of steps.</prompt>

  <goal>Every hold, approval, AP export and spend decision reads only class (a), (b) or (c) sources.</goal>

  <scope>
    165a (FIRST; uac-r2 priority):
    - Inventory every sprk_invoicesubmission column that a hold, approval, AP export or visibility decision reads, and classify each. Include `FinanceBaseValues.HeldSubmissionConditions`, `InvoiceApprovalService.IsHeldAsync`, `InvoiceOpenHolds`, the submission's `sprk_invoice` link, its reason, status and firm, and the re-run and persister reads.
    - Fix every column outside (a), (b) and (c). Choose per column:
      - field-secure it, Writers only, with the `sprk_sourceemaildocument` mechanics (SpaarkeMaster source, a script with -WhatIf, apply and -Verify, the owner's go for the dev apply);
      - or re-derive or cross-check it from a class (a) or (b) source, for example the outcome the persister recorded in the field-secured `sprk_findingsjson`, or the invoice's field-secured `sprk_firmhold`.
    - The held set must not be shrinkable by a user edit: a must-fire test for each hold source.
    165b:
    - (1) Approval refuses a line of unknown origin: the task 164 criterion "approval refuses a line of unknown origin", moved here in full.
    - (2) Status: approval, AP export and spend count an invoice as Approved, Sent to AP or Paid only when the matching server-written record exists, and otherwise refuse or hold it (409, a distinct code). The records: the approve Decision Record; the export batch or its record for Sent to AP; the paid record. Verify that each one is class (a) or (b). Spend (`FinanceBaseValues`) is ontology-r1's code: make the minimal change and list it for their review.
    - (3) Totals: approval and AP export check that the stored invoice totals equal `InvoiceTotalsCalculator` over the lines, and refuse on a mismatch (409, a distinct code).
    - (4) Pending spend (a confirmed defect found in the 165a review, not a known limit): both pending-spend paths (`FinanceBaseValues.cs` ~:416 anti-join, `FinanceRollupService.cs` ~:344) exclude every invoice `InvoiceBlockedHold` holds, so a user edit of a submission's status, reason code or link cannot make a held invoice count as pending spend. ontology-r1 owns `FinanceBaseValues`: minimal change, listed for their review. Must-fire per path with a must-not-fire control; one seed.
    Merge note: 165a puts the invoice's own-submission selection in one helper; 164a-4a moved `ReadSubmissionAsync` into `InvoiceFindingsDiff`. Whichever merges second calls the helper there.
  </scope>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>165b item 1, moved from task 164 verbatim:
    uac-r2 2026-11-06, part 164a-4a: approval refuses a line of unknown origin.
      - InvoiceApprovalService refuses (409, nothing written) an invoice with a Fee or Expense line that is neither
        (i) a linked submission's own line (`line.Id == InvoiceSubmissionPersister.LineIdFor(submissionId, sequence - 1)` for a submission
        linked to this invoice), nor (ii) the subject of an `add-line` Decision Record that names THIS invoice and THIS line id and was written
        by the BFF Add line service (app-only).
      - The reviewer-added marker in `sprk_extractionconfidence` is NOT an exemption. An added line's id is
        `AddedLineIdFor(decisionId)` (164a-2 fix round), and (ii) also requires `line.Id == AddedLineIdFor(record's decision id)`.
        The service creates the row with that id, which also gives the Q3 idempotency.
      - (ii) must be unforgeable. In the notes and the PR, cite the writer-only or append-only refusal of a user-created or user-updated
        `sprk_decisionrecord` through the generic BFF paths, and the role privileges on the table that close the direct path.
      - The line set is re-checked inside the approval's own row-version or lock scope. If it can't be, record a known limit stating what still holds.
      - The refusal logs a distinct reason code with the table and row id only.
      - Tests:
        - must-fire: a line of unknown origin (status Clean or Accepted) is refused;
        - must-fire: a line of unknown origin carrying the reviewer marker is refused;
        - must-fire: a line of unknown origin with a user-created `add-line` record is refused;
        - must-not-fire: intake lines plus an Add line line approve;
        - must-not-fire: D-96's same-invoice detach and re-attach approves.
      - One seed: drop the check.
      - Wording in commits, the PR and notes stays neutral: "approval refuses a line of unknown origin".</criterion>
    <criterion>165a ships first, in the same release as EB-D-200, and in every case before AP export is turned on in any environment (uac-r2 2026-11-06).</criterion>
    <criterion>The notes hold a table of every submission column read by a hold, approval, AP export or visibility decision, with the reader file:line, the class and the evidence. No column is left outside (a), (b) or (c).</criterion>
    <criterion>Must-fire, one for each of these, each with a must-not-fire control:
      - a hold source edited by a user does not release the hold;
      - a line of unknown origin is refused at approval;
      - a status set without its record is refused or held at approval, AP export and spend;
      - a stored total that differs from the line-derived total is refused at approval and AP export.
      One seed for each guard: drop the check.</criterion>
    <criterion>Refusals log a distinct reason code with the table and row id only.</criterion>
    <criterion>Field security applied to dev only with the owner's go typed in the ebilling session; uac-r2 is told before and after; provisioning gets the ordered prerequisite.</criterion>
    <criterion>The filtered unit suites (Finance, Submission, Invoice, ApExport, ExternalAccess) and ArchTests pass; the BFF builds; the publish delta is measured against a fresh master build.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A hold source cannot be made (a), (b) or (c) without changing D-101 behaviour visible to reviewers or firms: STOP and report.</trigger>
    <!-- 165a K6 resolved by EB-D-201 (owner 2026-11-06): the hold stands; task 096b closes the direct-create paths and cleans up the dev records. -->
  </escalation>
</task>
